2	#define SG_FUSED_SM90_PP_STAGE_DECODER_TC_CUH_
3	// ============================================================================
4	// csrc/fused/sm_90/pp_stage_decoder_tc.cuh — PIPELINE-PARALLEL stage kernels
5	// for the L3-TC decoder megakernel (design §4, task #25 phase-2, Lane C).
6	//
7	// THE CUT (design §4.1): PP splits the LAYER STACK across stages; each stage is
8	// its OWN persistent megakernel launch over its layer subset — the megakernel
9	// remains the unit of execution (P0→P1→B1→P2 fused inside each stage; we shard
10	// AROUND the fused step, never decompose it into ops). The acts-to-HBM DecActs
11	// design makes the boundary natural:
12	//   * FWD handoff  = acts.X_in[Lhi]  (bf16 [T,d]) — the boundary layer's n2
13	//     output, written by the EXISTING li+1<kLayers branch. Same-device loopback:
14	//     zero-copy (shared acts). Real PP: a P2P copy of exactly this region.
15	//   * BWD handoff  = dh_boundary (fp32 [T,d]) — the downstream stage's running
16	//     adjoint at its Llo input. fp32 ON PURPOSE: in the fused kernel this value
17	//     never rounds to bf16, so the fp32 carrier keeps the stage composition
18	//     BIT-IDENTICAL to the single-launch kernel (the loopback gate's assert).
19	//
20	// 1F1B / fwd-bwd split (design §4.1-4.2): a pipeline interleaves microbatches'
21	// fwd and bwd, so a stage exposes
22	//   * pp_decoder_stage_fwd_tc   — FWD-ONLY launch (single phase, no barriers):
23	//     P1-fwd tiles → boundary acts (+ nothing else; loss only exists on the
24	//     last stage's bwd pass).
25	//   * pp_decoder_stage_bwd_tc   — the FUSED fwd-RECOMPUTE + bwd + grad-assembly
26	//     launch: P0 → B0 → P1 (fwd<Llo,Lhi> re-runs to repopulate the per-CTA tile
27	//     scratch — per-tile recompute is the standard PP bwd pattern and is
28	//     BIT-identical here because the tile math is deterministic — then
29	//     bwd<Llo,Lhi> with dh_in/dh_out) → B1 → P2 over the OWNED tensors only
30	//     (dW split-K path identical to production, owned biases, embedding scan on
31	//     stage 0, owned LN-vec slots, loss on the last stage).
32	//   The last stage's 1F1B "fwd then immediately bwd" is exactly ONE
33	//   pp_decoder_stage_bwd_tc launch — the fused fwd+bwd unit is preserved there.
34	//
35	// OPTIMIZER: NOT here. PP composes with the established B2-seam cut (design
36	// §2.1/§2.2): each stage produces the reduced grad for its OWNED tensors; the
37	// DP/ZeRO collective dance + sharded_optimizer_kernel (bit-parity-proven by
38	// ef433ac DELIVERABLE 1) applies the update. A PP stage kernel therefore ends
39	// at its B2-equivalent ("owned grad assembled").
40	//
41	// TENSOR OWNERSHIP (dec_layout named_parameters() order):
42	//   stage owning layers [Llo,Lhi) owns tensors [2+12·Llo, 2+12·Lhi)
43	//   (12 tensors per layer: in_w,in_b,out_w,out_b,n1w,n1b,n2w,n2b,ff0w,ff0b,
44	//    ff2w,ff2b); stage 0 additionally owns {0,1} (tok,pos); the LAST stage
45	//   additionally owns {26,27,28,29} (final norm γ/β + head w/b).
46	//   dW specs (4 per layer + head): spec s ∈ [4·Llo, 4·Lhi) (+ spec 8 on last).
47	//   LN-vec slots: v ∈ [4·Llo, 4·Lhi) (+ {8,9} on last).
48	//
49	// REQUIRES the layer-range patch (.phase2/patches/0001-dectc-layer-range-pp
50	// .patch) on model_stage_decoder_tc.cuh — gated LOUDLY below, no silent
51	// degradation. This header is NEW (not in the production build glob); it is
52	// JIT-compiled by tests/hw/pp_stage_binding.cu.
53	// ============================================================================
54	
55	// The wgmma stage substrate + (transitively) the patched tile functions.
