1	// csrc/fused/sm_90/mega_vit_real_adamw_tc_launcher.cu — R2.4 WIRED tensor-core
2	// host-launcher TU for the TRUE L3 fused (vit × adamw) megakernel.
3	//
4	// Twin of mega_decoder_real_adamw_tc_launcher.cu for ViT (see that file's header
5	// for the full rationale). The shipped scalar launcher mega_vit_real_adamw.cu
6	// compiles the SCALAR cell only; the Fork-B TC driver mega_vit_real_adamw_tc.cu
7	// owns its own PYBIND11_MODULE and is dropped from _ops. This TU is the missing
8	// seam: globbed INTO _ops (no own pybind module), compiled -DSG_TUNED_GEMM_IMPL=1
9	// so it links the wgmma branch of fused_vit_megakernel.cuh, exposing ONE
10	// non-template host launcher with a plain pointers/ints + FusedScalars boundary
11	// (dispatch.cpp extern-decls it with the mirror structs). Calls ONLY
12	// launch_fused_vit_megakernel_tc → never instantiates the scalar launcher
13	// template → CANNOT collide with the scalar TU in _ops. Owns its own TC-sized
14	// activations/grad workspace (vit_tc_workspace_floats != the scalar nCTA*total
15	// partials), so dispatch.cpp passes no workspace for the TC path.
16	//
17	// ViT input is FLOAT image patches with int targets (dispatch.cpp bit-reinterprets
18	// the targets out of the trailing float slots and passes a real const int* here).
19	//
20	// HONESTY: the REAL bf16 wgmma path (HGMMA in SASS, validated by
