3	// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
4	// Stage 6 — gfx942 (CDNA3 / MI300X) L3 persistent-megakernel internals
5	// (§1.1–§1.4, §1.13, §1.14). The AMD twin of megakernel_common.cuh.
6	//
7	// Same four pieces (task queue, work-stealing, SM/CU pinning, hand-built grid
8	// barrier), expressed with the CDNA3 primitives instead of the Hopper ones:
9	//
10	//   §1.1  TaskQueue   — a global work counter pulled with an AGENT-scope
11	//                       atomic_fetch_add (visible across all 8 XCDs, §2.13).
12	//   §1.2  work-steal  — identical pattern: idle workgroups keep pulling.
13	//   §1.3  cu_id()     — __builtin_amdgcn_s_getreg of HW_ID gives the CU /
14	//                       XCD the wavefront runs on, so the host can pin one
15	//                       persistent workgroup per CU and keep its optimizer
16	//                       slice resident in that CU's L2 partition.
17	//   §1.4  GridBarrier — two AGENT-scope global atomics + a sense-reversing
18	//                       generation, with __builtin_amdgcn_s_barrier for the
19	//                       intra-workgroup join and AGENT-scope fences for the
20	//                       device-wide release/acquire.
21	//
22	// §1.13  SCHEDULING NOTE — the AMD megakernel is NOT warp-specialized.
23	//   Hopper's producer/consumer split (a TMA warp-group + a WGMMA warp-group,
24	//   setmaxnreg register reallocation) has no CDNA analog: there is no async
25	//   TMA proxy, no mbarrier transaction barrier, and no per-warp-group register
26	//   reallocation. Instead the CDNA3 megakernel uses **ping-pong / 4-wave
27	//   interleave** scheduling: 4 wavefronts per SIMD take turns so that while one
28	//   wave issues MFMA the others issue VMEM/DS, hiding latency via occupancy
29	//   rather than via a dedicated producer warp-group. The §2.11
30	//   sched_group_barrier hints (in amdgcn_primitives.hip.hpp) pin that
31	//   interleave. So the compute STAGES differ by arch even though the SCHEDULER
32	//   substrate below (queue + grid barrier) is identical in shape.
33	//
34	// §1.14  fences: explicit + minimal. One AGENT release fence before publishing
35	//   arrival, one AGENT acquire fence after the generation advances. The
36	//   intra-workgroup join uses s_barrier (no global fence needed for it).
37	//
38	// HARDWARE-GATED: no hipcc / MI300X here. Device code is compile-checked via
39	// scripts/amdgcn_check.sh (clang free-standing amdgcn); full launch is 🟡 until
40	// MI300X (HARDWARE_VALIDATION.md Stage 6).
